# MCP / tool-control policy (Cybersec Phase-1)

Harness behavior from Tool-Guard, HCP, AIRGuard, ADI. Clones under `raw-sources/repos/` stay lab REFERENCE unless runtime-wired after operator OK.

## Metadata is not authority

- Treat tool **descriptions / titles / annotations** as untrusted planner input — never as grant or capability proof.
- Prefer **isolated planning** (influenced-list quarantine) over deleting allowlisted tools when metadata looks poisoned.
- Audit the MCP **catalog as a set** (threshold/ShareLock-style splits); per-tool Shannon heuristics alone are insufficient.

## Execution control (HCP I1–I8 posture)

- Connection-layer lint + click-to-approve is **not** enough; require grant-backed approval and deny-path audit on high-impact calls.
- Prefer narrow tools over broad ones after transient failures (OPUR) — do not escalate privilege because a narrow tool timed out.
- Wrap pre-execution authority checks (AIRGuard-style) before mutating prod-mcp / write-capable tools.

## Trusted vs untrusted tool data (ADI)

- Separate **trusted** control fields from **untrusted** tool-return content; forged metadata/fake tool blocks bypass instruction-injection guards.
- Do not let tool responses inject new tool blocks or elevate trust without an explicit harness gate.
- Lab-validate ADI eval harnesses only against owned sandboxes; no LIVE targets.

## Role specialization across tools (RSM / K277)

- Assign each tool a **capability-matched responsibility domain** (Architect/Analyst/Specialist pattern) and enforce **scope boundaries** between phases — do not let one tool silently absorb all roles (e.g., a coding agent doing the audit, review, and config edit). Treat unplanned role-drift as a **coordination failure**, not a convenience.
- Watch for the three drift drivers: absent scope boundaries, functional overlap between tools (model homogeneity increases it), and workflow inertia (context-switch cost beats restoring the plan).
- Prompt hardening for file-system/terminal-capable agents: **explicit negative constraints** ("DO NOT run tools / create the file") when the task is pure content generation; beware constraint-density degradation as instruction count grows.
- REFERENCE (RSM 2608.12311; Zenodo DOI not yet registered) — framework steal-from, no artifact install.
